    "name_raw": "Obscuring Beacon",
    "definition_type_raw": "Combat",
    "source_book_raw": "Heroes of the Darklands pg. 5",
    "definition_raw": "Source Heroes of the Darklands pg. 5\nYou use light to disrupt your foes’ darkness-adapted vision.\n\nBenefit: When you’re holding a light source in an area that is otherwise dim or darker, foes within the normal or bright light radius shed by your light source take a –1 penalty on attack rolls against other targets that are also within the radius of your light. Blind creatures aren’t affected by this feat.",
